WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.275
Unit 1 is the guide's Step 5.

2
00:00:02.275 --> 00:00:04.750
The project owner does two things once.

3
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:07.402
Enable the Service Health
A P I on the project,

4
00:00:07.402 --> 00:00:11.775
and grant the reader's group the
Personalized Service Health Viewer role.

5
00:00:11.775 --> 00:00:13.013
Then two steps.

6
00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:16.343
One: cross-check the list
with Google's own command,

7
00:00:16.343 --> 00:00:21.299
G cloud service health events list, for
the project, in the global location.

8
00:00:21.299 --> 00:00:24.537
Two: collect, with the
provider set to Google.

9
00:00:24.537 --> 00:00:29.212
For a whole organization, set the settings
file's Google scope to organization,

10
00:00:29.212 --> 00:00:31.513
and grant the role on the organization.

11
00:00:31.513 --> 00:00:35.876
Otherwise, grant it at the project:
the viewer role on the organization,

12
00:00:35.876 --> 00:00:39.487
for a project read, is more read
scope than the reader needs.

13
00:00:39.487 --> 00:00:42.711
The gate validates when products
and locations come from

14
00:00:42.711 --> 00:00:45.599
the event's impacts, and
closed incidents are closed.

15
00:00:45.599 --> 00:00:48.600
The gate owner is the
Google Cloud project owner.
